== a parent without a finalizer holds a child with one: the finalizer comes before the parent's tp_dealloc (CPython: after it has begun)
['__del__'] [1000040] handed on, finalized: True
at its real end: ['__del__'] [1000041]
== two instances of a class that only they lead to. A dead parent holds the one, which keeps the class. The other ends as a Node beside it (CPython: as what it is)
Py_TYPE(self) was Node itself in the tp_dealloc of the one that nobody holds: True
[1000042, 1000043, 1000044]
== a tp_traverse asks about what it holds. Nothing is made in the middle of a collection, so Py_TYPE() is NULL where the type might have to be (CPython: never)
a str: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 0, and gc says 0
an int: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 0, and gc says 0
a list: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
a tuple of numbers: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 0, and gc says 0
an instance: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
a class: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
a function: Py_TYPE() is NULL: True; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 0; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
a built-in function: Py_TYPE() is NULL: True; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 0; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
an instance of a class that derives from list: Py_TYPE() is NULL: True; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 0; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
a typed array of JS's: Py_TYPE() is NULL: True; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 0; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
a tuple with one in it: Py_TYPE() is NULL: False; Py_IS_TYPE(it, that): 1; it is tracked: 1, and gc says 1
